# SMB 3.1.1+ enforcement — implementation in Normain

Goal: make every Azure Storage Account allow **only SMB 3.1.1** for Azure Files, to pass the Vanta test `azure-storage-account-file-share-smb-protocol-version-3-1-1-or-higher-only`. 20 accounts currently fail (sitting at Azure default, which permits SMB 2.1/3.0).

Repo: `~/dev/projects/normain`. Provider: `hashicorp/azurerm >= 4.51` (supports `share_properties.smb.versions`).

The Terraform change to restrict SMB version is, on each `azurerm_storage_account`:

```hcl
share_properties {
  smb {
    versions = ["SMB3.1.1"]
  }
}
```

Valid `versions` values: `SMB2.1`, `SMB3.0`, `SMB3.1.1`. Listing only `SMB3.1.1` drops the older two. Safe on all account kinds (blob-only, StorageV2, Premium FileStorage); does not affect the existing NFS share.

