## Required changes

### Change 1 — Group A (covers 8/20)
Add the `share_properties` block to the 4 resources:
- `terraform/modules/azure/main.tf` → `uploaded_files`, `artifacts`, `data_sources`
- `terraform/modules/azure/audit.tf` → `audit_immutable`

One module edit; both `app-production` and `app-development` inherit it on `terraform apply`.

`terraform plan` should show only an in-place update (`~`) of `share_properties` on each — no replacement.

### Change 2 — Group B state backends (6 accounts)
These exist already and are created imperatively, so two parts:
1. **New accounts going forward:** add to `createStorageBackend.ts`, after `az storage account create`:
   ```
   az storage account file-service-properties update \
     --account-name ${accountName} \
     --resource-group ${resourceGroup} \
     --versions SMB3.1.1
   ```
2. **Existing accounts (one-time):** run the same `file-service-properties update --versions SMB3.1.1` once per account: normaintfappproduction, normaintfappdevelopment, normaintfidentity, normainfglobal, storagenormainiacprod01, storagenormainiacdev20.

(Alternative: `terraform import` each into HCL and apply Change-1-style blocks — heavier, gives drift detection.)

### Change 3 — Group B out-of-band (rps*, stwinvm*, stsublogarch, normainstorage = 6 accounts)
Not managed by any code. Per account, one-time:
```
az storage account file-service-properties update \
  --account-name <name> --resource-group <rg> --versions SMB3.1.1
```
RGs: rps* → `rg-normain-{prod-01,dev-20}`; stwinvm* → `rg-normain-{prod-01,dev-20}`; stsublogarch → `rg-normain-global`; normainstorage → `Normain`.
(Optional follow-up: bring these under IaC so they don't drift back.)

